      "content": "The most equitable way to distribute affordable housing units is through a lottery system, as it ensures that every applicant has an equal chance of securing a unit, regardless of income level or proximity to transit. This approach prevents the wealthy from buying up all the desirable units and leaves the door open for long-term residents who may not have the financial means to afford market-rate housing. By making the selection process random, you can ensure that the most vulnerable members of the community have access to these much-needed resources.",
